    "c.el.t": "Electricity bill discount",
    "c.el.d": "For: {who}. National Insurance usually sends the name to the electric company, and the discount is given automatically. But the discount is linked to the electricity contract, so in a new home the contract must be in the name of the entitled person.",
    "c.el.how": "When you move the electricity account, tell the representative you're entitled to the discount. After the first bill, check that the discount appears. If not, contact the electric company. You can get a refund for past bills too.",
    "c.elw.seniorSupp": "old-age pension with income supplement", "c.elw.lowIncome": "income support or alimony", "c.elw.kidDisability": "disabled child allowance",
    "c.elw.nursing": "long-term care allowance", "c.elw.idf": "IDF disabled veterans or victims of hostile action", "c.elw.holocaust": "Holocaust survivors (by income)", "c.elw.soldier": "lone soldiers",
    "c.wa.t": "Reduced rate for each person in the home", "c.wa.d": "Each person living in the home gets 3.5 m³ of water a month at the low rate. If you don't report how many people live there, you pay more.",
    "c.wa.how": "Tell the water corporation how many people live in the home, in the same request as moving the account.",
    "c.wm.t": "Extra water at the reduced rate, for medical reasons", "c.wm.d": "In some medical situations you can get more water at the low rate.",
    "c.wm.how": "Ask the water corporation about an \"extra allocation for special populations\" and attach a medical confirmation.",
    "c.kd.t": "Daycare or family daycare subsidy", "c.kd.d": "The state helps pay for a recognized daycare or family daycare. If you move to a new daycare, make sure it's recognized and your request is up to date.",
    "c.kd.how": "Apply on the Ministry of Labor website, after you choose a daycare in your new city.",
    "c.kr.t": "Kindergarten or school registration", "c.kr.d": "With children, check early whether you need to move their registration to the new city.", "c.kr.how": "Contact the municipality's education department.",
    "c.tx.t": "Income tax credit for living in an eligible town",
    "c.tx.d": "If {city} is on the list of eligible towns, you get an income tax credit after 12 months in a row of living there. The credit also covers the time from when you moved in.",
    "c.tx.how": "Check whether the town is on the list. Employees give their employer Form 101 and proof of residence from the local authority (Form 1312A). Self-employed people claim it in their annual report.",
    "c.sa.t": "Paying arnona for the whole year in advance", "c.sa.d": "Many municipalities give a small discount if you pay the whole year in advance. Some also give a discount for a standing order.",
    "c.sa.how": "Ask the arnona department when you open the account.",
    "c.se.t": "Private electricity supplier", "c.se.d": "You can buy electricity from a private supplier for less than the Israel Electric rate. The meter, the grid and repairs stay with Israel Electric.",
    "c.se.how": "Compare plans. Some plans need a smart meter. Moving is a good time to decide.",
    "c.sc.t": "A new price for internet and TV", "c.sc.d": "When you move a service to a new address, companies are willing to give a better price so you don't leave.",
    "c.sc.how": "Before you confirm the move, check prices with other companies and ask for a better offer.",
    "c.si.t": "New home insurance", "c.si.d": "The premium depends on the address, floor and size of the home. It's a good time to compare offers.", "c.si.how": "Ask several companies for quotes before you update.",

